abstract: >-
  A report on fine-tuning a character LoRA for MiniMax H3, a 33B omni-modal
  video generation model. Contrary to the common assumption that GPU VRAM is
  the limiting factor, the measured peak VRAM during training was 3,959 MiB
  while training failed on hosts with 50 GB of system RAM and succeeded on a
  host with 188 GB. The trained adapter transfers across quantization formats
  and runs inference within 9.3 GB of VRAM on a consumer GPU.
